{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Write one file below runtime/files/shared, creating missing parent directories. content is raw DataBytes, a UTF-8 string, or - from a peer - {stream, size}: the caller opened a peer stream (peer.service.new_stream), and this command joins it as the calling peer (nn_session.username), reads exactly size bytes (30 s stall limit) and refuses a short stream. Every source is written to a temporary file beside the target and renamed into place, so a failed upload never replaces a good file. Returns {path, size, created} or {status err, code, msg} (400 bad input or short stream, 405 target is a directory, 502 stream not joinable, 500 filesystem). Rejects empty paths, traversal, absolute paths, and symlinks via resolve_path. Open to admin and the files-write group; used by files.dav locally and by a peer's files.peerdav PUT.","groups":"files-write","import":"use crate::files::files::resolve_path::resolve_path;\nuse ndata::databytes::DataBytes;\nuse std::io::Write;\nuse std::panic::{catch_unwind, AssertUnwindSafe};","params":[{"desc":"Destination share-relative file path below runtime/files/shared. Missing parents are created.","name":"path","type":"String"},{"desc":"The file's content: raw bytes (DataBytes), a UTF-8 string, or - from a peer - an object {stream: <peer stream id the caller opened with peer.service.new_stream>, size: <byte count>} whose bytes are read from that stream.","name":"content","type":"Any"},{"desc":"Request metadata filled in by the framework; its username names the calling peer whose stream is joined. Pass an empty object for bytes or string content.","name":"nn_session","type":"JSONObject"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"hhyigz1a1ad1c6753s1d7","readers":["files-write"],"time":1794360511416,"username":"system","writers":[]}